      <p>
        The same component in a column too narrow for a rail, which is what a phone gets. It becomes
        a closed disclosure so the list stays reachable without pushing the article down, and it
        sits in flow under the title and byline rather than beside them. Native
        <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> — no JavaScript involved.
      </p>
      <div class="toc-narrow-demo">
        <TableOfContents
          headings={sections.map((s) => ({ depth: 2, slug: s.id, text: s.label }))}
        />
      </div>

      <h3 class="subhead">Nesting</h3>
      <p>Each level indents against the shared rail rather than starting a new one:</p>
      <TableOfContents
        headings={[
          { depth: 2, text: 'Getting started', slug: 'getting-started' },
